					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-610445#post-3934021</guid>
				<title>On a lighter note...</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-610445/a-canticle-for-bright#post-3934021</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 27 Aug 2018 15:27:08 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Quinn Mallory</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2054862</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Zhakh returned to his chambers, still uncertain. To begin again, to spend years more in service of&#8230;</p> <p>No.</p> <p>He found a piece of parchment, and a pen, and began to write a list of everything he thought wrong with the actions of the Holy Foundation. As his candles burned low, he wrote on, and on, hand aching, knowing this was heresy, but also knowing that he had to do what he believed was right.</p> <p>As the Sun began to rise, he finished his work. It was a long list; he looked back over the items, checking that he hadn't missed a number anywhere. No, he hadn't - there were ninety-five.</p> <p>Now, to nail this somewhere where people could see it&#8230;</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
